### Step 1: send the 3 token requests first. Step 2: send requests 1-5.

# @name login_user
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "user",
  "password": "user"
}

###

# @name login_manager
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "manager",
  "password": "manager"
}

###

# @name login_admin
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "admin",
  "password": "admin"
}

###

###1. ADMIN JWT: GET all audit notes -> 200
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/audit
Authorization: Bearer {{login_admin.response.body.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###2. ADMIN JWT: GET one audit note -> 200
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/audit/1
Authorization: Bearer {{login_admin.response.body.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###3. ADMIN JWT: GET audit notes of user 'manager' -> 200
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/audit?username=manager
Authorization: Bearer {{login_admin.response.body.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###4. MANAGER JWT: GET own audit notes -> 200
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/audit/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login_manager.response.body.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###5. USER JWT: GET all audit notes -> 403 Forbidden
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/audit
Authorization: Bearer {{login_user.response.body.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###
